    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0316" n="1050" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1050"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lima, Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received August 22.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 407.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that as the
                    regular session of Congress opens to-morrow (the 28th instant), I have placed a
                    note in the hands of his excellency Señor Larrabrue y Unanne, minister of
                    foreign <pb facs="0317" n="1051" xml:id="pg1051"/> relations here, in reference
                    to the long-pending claim of citizens of the United States, upon the Government
                    of Peru, known as the Hydro-graphic Commission of the Amazon, as per my inclosed
                    communication.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d262-a1.xml" xpointer="d262-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
